{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "nodeID": "212",
   "text": "Emerging economies face the same shocks — do they need the same response?",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "question",
   "toulmin": "framing",
   "oper": "framing",
   "localID": "setser_mar_31_20#Q"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "213",
   "text": "Shocks can offset one another; swap lines fund dollar balance sheets, not balance-of-payments gaps",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_mar_31_20#P1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "214",
   "text": "The external balance sheet is the right thing to sort countries by",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "hidden_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_mar_31_20#P2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "215",
   "text": "\"contrary to a forecast that I made with Dr. Roubini back in 2005\" — private credit intermediation broke down before central banks lost their appetite for intervention",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "revised_prior",
   "toulmin": "revision",
   "oper": "revision",
   "localID": "setser_mar_31_20#P3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "216",
   "text": "Brent under $25, below almost every exporter's breakeven; Saudi reserves ~$500bn; GCC sovereign funds over $1tn; copper at multiyear lows",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_mar_31_20#E1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "217",
   "text": "Truman on IMF lending capacity; Landers, Lee and Morris on callable capital; Hagan and Buchheit on maturity extension; Carstens and the BIS on trade finance",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_source",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_mar_31_20#E2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "218",
   "text": "The same four shocks land very differently depending on the external balance sheet",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_mar_31_20#M1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "219",
   "text": "Swap lines solve dollar funding, but were never designed to cover a balance-of-payments shortfall",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_mar_31_20#M2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "220",
   "text": "Countries with strong external balance sheets can weather this themselves if they act decisively",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_mar_31_20#C1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "221",
   "text": "Three types — reserve-rich commodity exporters, Asian surplus creditors, weak external balance sheets — and the last splits again into trade finance and balance-of-payments need",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "case_type",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_mar_31_20#C2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "222",
   "text": "\"Different problems require different solutions\" — when private capital retreats, the official sector must advance",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "main_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.final",
   "localID": "setser_mar_31_20#K"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "223",
   "text": "Draw down buffers; central bank backstop plus swap lines; mobilise trade finance; SDR allocation, larger IMF capacity, MDB callable capital, payment deferral",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "recommendation",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.final",
   "localID": "setser_mar_31_20#REC"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "224",
   "text": "Private creditors would rather be paid — \"this will take goodwill\"",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "opposing_view",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_mar_31_20#X"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "225",
   "text": "SDRs are allocated by quota rather than need, so they are insufficient alone; MDB capital would need legislation",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "caveat",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_mar_31_20#QF"
  },
  {
